### 2. What You Can Deduct (Above-the-Line & Business Deductions)
Even though you are taking the standard deduction, you can still claim "above-the-line" adjustments to your income and business expenses:
*   **Student Loan Interest:** You paid $4,100, but the IRS caps the student loan interest deduction at **$2,500** per return. Because your Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) is around $105,000, you are well below the phase-out limit ($155,000 for MFJ), so you can deduct the full $2,500.
*   **Unreimbursed Expenses ($1,350):** 
